|> Exercise
    handle=_inverse_signatures_

    |> CodexSuggestion

        If $f : [\A] \ra [\B]$ is invertible (cf. Exercise >>_inverse_graph_introduction_),
        what are the signatures of

        $$
        f^{-1},\qquad f^{-1}\circ f,\qquad f\circ f^{-1},\qquad (f^{-1})'?
        $$

        (Assume the inverse is differentiable for the last part.)

    |> Solution
        |> CodexSuggestion

            The inverse swaps the input and output units. Thus:

            $$
            \begin{aligned}
            f^{-1} &: [\B] \ra [\A] \\
            f^{-1}\circ f &: [\A] \ra [\A]\up{1.35} \\
            f\circ f^{-1} &: [\B] \ra [\B]\up{1.35} \\
            (f^{-1})' &: [\B] \ra [\A/\B]\up{1.35}
            \end{aligned}
            $$
